## Assumption challenge
Candidate vertices considered:
- runners
- gaps
- fixed circle sections
- section boundaries
- wall-crossing events
- residue/CRT fibers
- cover arcs
- Fourier/cyclotomic modes
- matroid contact circuits
- proof obligations / sidecar columns
Chosen vertices are proof obligations because the quotient preserves the LRC predicate only after unit contacts, covering floor, 2-adic magnitude, apex ramification, and hinge data are all either retained or explicitly discharged.
